####### # Setup #######
$name = randomPerson(); $initial = random(12,17); $rate = random(10,15); $final = 100; Context("LinearRelation")->variables->are(t => 'Real'); $equation = LinearRelation("$initial + $rate t = $final");
############################# # Exercise Group Introduction #############################
BEGIN_PGML Write an equation to model the scenario. There is no need to solve the equation.
END_PGML
###### # Body ######
BEGIN_PGML [$name] puts a pot of water from the tap onto the stove and turns the burner all the way up. The water temperature starts at [`[$initial]\,^{\circ}C`] and climbs steadily up to the boiling point of [`[$final]\,^{\circ}C\text{,}`] raising at a rate of [`[$rate]\,\frac{^{\circ}C}{\text{min}}\text{.}`] How long will it take for the pot to boil? Write an equation to model this scenario. There is no need to solve it.
[@KeyboardInstructions('Use [|t|]* as the variable.')@]**
[_]{$equation}{20}
END_PGML
